---
import ChartScale from './ChartScale.astro';
---
<section id="forecast-view" class="view" hidden>
  <header class="page-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / CASH-FLOW PROJECTIONS</p><h1>A little foresight.</h1><p class="subtitle">Explore up to five years of cash flow. Compare methods and see how your assumptions change the path.</p></div><ChartScale id="forecast-scale" /></header>
  <div class="forecast-layout">
    <article class="card assumptions"><div class="card-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">START HERE</p><h2>Your starting point</h2></div></div>
    <label>Starting balances<select id="balance-source"><option value="manual">Enter a combined starting point</option><option value="accounts">Use saved account balances</option></select></label>
    <p id="balance-source-note" class="input-note">Enter combined balances or choose your dated account balances.</p>
    <label>Available cash <span>NOK</span><input id="cash" type="number" step="0.01" placeholder="Enter current balance"></label>
      <p class="input-note">Cash you can spend, excluding the savings reserve below.</p>
      <label>Savings reserve <span>NOK</span><input id="savings" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" placeholder="0"></label>
      <label>Minimum cash buffer <span>NOK</span><input id="buffer" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" placeholder="0"></label>
      <label>Balance date<input id="balance-date" type="date"></label>
      <div class="form-divider"></div><h3>Monthly assumptions</h3>
      <label>Use history from<select id="lookback"><option value="1">Last complete month</option><option value="3" selected>Last 3 complete months</option><option value="6">Last 6 complete months</option><option value="12">Last 12 complete months</option></select></label>
      <p id="baseline-caption" class="input-note"></p>
      <label>Regular income <span>NOK / month</span><input id="income" type="number" min="0" step="0.01"></label>
      <label>Spending & bills <span>NOK / month</span><input id="expense" type="number" min="0" step="0.01"></label>
      <label>Savings & investments <span>NOK / month</span><input id="saving" type="number" min="0" step="0.01"></label>
      <p class="input-note">Includes recorded contributions from available cash into reserves and investments, including accounts you track manually. Investment values and returns are not projected.</p>
      <button id="reset-baseline" class="text-button">↺ Use averages from history</button>
      <button id="large-payments" class="text-button">Review large historical payments →</button>
    </article>
    <div class="forecast-results">
      <article class="card"><div class="card-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR POSSIBLE PATH</p><h2>Cash over time</h2></div><div class="forecast-time-controls"><label class="forecast-horizon">History shown<select id="forecast-history"><option value="0">Future only</option><option value="1">1 month</option><option value="3" selected>3 months</option><option value="6">6 months</option><option value="12">12 months</option><option value="24">24 months</option></select></label><label class="forecast-horizon">Forecast horizon<select id="forecast-horizon">{Array.from({ length: 60 }, (_, i) => i + 1).map(months => <option value={months} selected={months === 3}>{months} {months === 1 ? 'month' : 'months'}{months % 12 === 0 ? ` · ${months / 12} ${months === 12 ? 'year' : 'years'}` : ''}</option>)}</select></label><button id="open-forecast-methods" type="button" class="outline-button forecast-method-trigger" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="forecast-method-dialog">Projection methods <span id="forecast-method-count" class="muted small"></span></button></div></div>
        <div class="scenario-row"><span class="muted small">Try a scenario</span><button data-scenario="same" class="scenario selected">Current pace</button><button data-scenario="less" class="scenario">Spend 10% less</button><button data-scenario="more" class="scenario">Spend 10% more</button></div>
        <p id="forecast-history-note" class="input-note"></p>
        <div id="forecast-chart" class="forecast-chart"></div>
        <p id="forecast-chart-history-note" class="input-note"></p>
        <p class="input-note">Longer horizons amplify differences between assumptions. These lines are alternative projections, not confidence bounds or probabilities.</p>
        <dl id="forecast-stats" class="statistics-grid statistics-grid-three forecast-stat-cards"></dl>
        <div class="scenario-inputs"><label>Monthly spending change <span>NOK / month</span><input id="adjustment" type="number" step="0.01" value="0"><small>Negative means spending less.</small></label><label>One-off expense in month 1 <span>NOK</span><input id="one-off" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="0"></label></div>
        <div id="forecast-message" class="forecast-message" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card"><div class="card-heading"><h2>Compare outcomes</h2><span class="muted small">All visible methods · before reserve withdrawals</span></div><div id="forecast-comparison"></div></article>
      <article class="card"><div class="card-heading"><h2>Month by month</h2><span class="muted small">Rolling monthly estimates</span></div><div id="forecast-table"></div></article>
      <article class="card" aria-labelledby="scenario-insights-title"><div class="card-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">PUT THE SCENARIO IN CONTEXT</p><h2 id="scenario-insights-title">What shapes your forecast</h2></div></div><dl id="scenario-insights" class="statistics-grid statistics-grid-three"></dl></article>
      <details class="method-note"><summary>How this forecast works</summary><p>The baseline uses the average of complete months before the earlier of the balance month and latest transaction month. Regular income uses rows marked as salary or “Inntekt”. Other incoming money, refunds, and interest do not become recurring income automatically. All non-transfer outflows are included in spending or savings contributions.</p><p>Cash = starting cash + regular income − spending − savings contributions − spending change. The one-off expense is subtracted in month 1. Savings reserve is shown separately and is not automatically withdrawn. Internal transfers are excluded. Mark one-off historical transactions in Transactions to leave them out of the baseline.</p><p>Your scenario holds monthly inputs constant. Historical average, last month, and exponential smoothing estimate each of income, spending and savings separately from the selected complete months, then hold those estimates constant. Smoothing starts from the first complete month and rounds each update to integer øre. Seasonal repeat uses the last 12 complete months and repeats them by calendar month, even for horizons beyond a year. History ends before the earlier of the balance month and latest transaction month. Months without recorded activity inside that history count as zero; imports may be incomplete. Manual monthly inputs affect your scenario and unchanged assumptions only. Spending changes and the month-one expense apply to your scenario and all history methods; unchanged assumptions omits both. This estimate does not model payday, bill dates, interest, tax changes, or daily cash lows. End-of-month estimates can look healthy even if a bill is due before payday. It is a scenario calculation, not a bank balance or a guarantee. Coincident lines mean methods produced the same balances; inspect the chart figures or comparison tables for each method.</p><p>Chart history is reconstructed backwards from your starting cash using recorded non-transfer cash movements. It includes historical one-offs and all incoming money, regardless of forecast exclusions. These are not observed bank balances. Missing payments or a gap between the latest transaction and balance date can make this reconstruction incomplete. The History shown control changes the chart only; Use history from controls the estimation window.</p><p>Method background: <a href="https://otexts.com/fpp3/simple-methods.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">simple forecasting methods</a> and <a href="https://otexts.com/fpp3/ses.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">exponential smoothing</a> in Forecasting: Principles and Practice.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
  <dialog id="forecast-method-dialog" aria-labelledby="forecast-method-dialog-title" aria-describedby="forecast-method-dialog-note">
    <form method="dialog">
      <div class="dialog-heading"><h2 id="forecast-method-dialog-title">Projection methods</h2><button type="submit" class="icon-button" aria-label="Close projection methods">×</button></div>
      <p id="forecast-method-dialog-note" class="input-note">Your scenario stays visible. Select methods to compare on the same chart. Changes are applied and saved as you select.</p>
      <fieldset class="forecast-methods"><legend>Compare projection methods</legend><div id="forecast-method-options"></div></fieldset>
      <div class="dialog-actions"><button type="submit" class="primary-button">Done</button></div>
    </form>
  </dialog>
</section>
